The plate is square, roughly 26 cm across. It is photographed sideways. Six small reddish-brown pieces sit on it, and they look like chorizo or cured sausage chunks, each about 3 cm long and 2.5 cm wide. A cylinder of that size is about 15 cm³, so each piece weighs roughly 12–15 g. Six pieces come to about 80 g. Some pieces are smaller, so I settled on about 70 g.

Chorizo, cooked, is about 400 kcal/100 g. Other sausage is about 300, so I used 380 for chorizo-like sausage.

